**Compare**: I = (9 V − 1.8 V) / (1 kΩ + the LED's 12 Ω) ≈ **7.1 mA**.
- Voltage across the ammeter = 0.1 Ω × 7.1 mA ≈ **0.71 mV**, so it hardly changes the circuit;
- with the leads swapped it reads ≈ −7.1 mA;
- across the LED, the LED is shorted and goes dark, and the meter reads 9 V / 1 kΩ ≈ 9 mA — not the LED's current, but the current after the short.
